WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.340
"Using Thylakoids to Suppress
Hunger and Boost GLP-1"

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.507
The cells that produce

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.810
the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.478
in response to calorie exposure

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:13.113
are concentrated
all the way down

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.182
at the end
of our digestive tract,

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:16.350
which is why our appetites

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.386
are not suppressed very much
these days.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.921
The majority
of the calories we eat

00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:23.090
are absorbed early
in our digestive tract;

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.492
so, they never make it down
far enough.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.262
When we eat a donut,
its fat, sugar, and starch

00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:30.364
get absorbed quickly, high up,

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:32.332
before reaching the part
of our digestive tract

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.134
where we produce
most of the hormone

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.903
that suppresses our appetite.

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:38.505
So, from a GLP-1 standpoint,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.908
it’s like we never ate
much of anything.

00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:44.878
No wonder we reach for donut #2.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.949
How can we eat a donut
and still get GLP-1 activation?

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:50.384
Surgery!

00:00:50.384 --> 00:00:52.452
Bariatric surgery
can involve cutting out

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.288
part of our small intestine

00:00:54.288 --> 00:00:55.622
so some of the donut calories

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.659
may reach the end of it
after all.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:01.962
What if you want to eat a donut,
still get GLP-1 activation,

00:01:01.962 --> 00:01:04.831
and keep your anatomy intact?

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.999
Drugs!

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.769
By injecting GLP-1
mimicking drugs, like Ozempic,

00:01:08.769 --> 00:01:12.773
you can get GLP-1 activation
no matter what you eat.

00:01:12.773 --> 00:01:15.676
You could also take
the starch-blocker drug acarbose

00:01:15.676 --> 00:01:18.045
to slow the digestion
of carbohydrates,

00:01:18.045 --> 00:01:22.449
or the fat-blocker drug orlistat
to slow the digestion of fats.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.551
But what if you want
GLP-1 activation

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:26.853
without drugs or surgery?

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.590
Well, you could try
not eating donuts.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.526
Ancestral humans
might have consumed

00:01:32.526 --> 00:01:34.962
as much as 100 grams
of fiber daily.

00:01:34.962 --> 00:01:37.064
That’s about six times

00:01:37.064 --> 00:01:39.032
what most of us are getting
these days.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.735
We evolved eating massive
amounts of whole plant foods,

00:01:41.735 --> 00:01:44.071
the only place
fiber is found in abundance.

00:01:44.071 --> 00:01:45.973
So, by eating
the way nature intended,

00:01:45.973 --> 00:01:49.142
we can release GLP-1
the way nature intended,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.312
which helps explain why
a whole food, plant-based diet

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.414
is one of the most powerful
weight loss interventions

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.416
ever published.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.453
But what do we do
about our cravings?

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.221
What are some
therapeutic approaches

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:01.989
to addressing them?

00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:03.757
Well, there are drugs,
of course,

00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:05.892
but in terms
of food-based interventions,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.362
there are thylakoids,

00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:10.330
which are just the
chlorophyll-rich membranes

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.633
inside leaves where
photosynthesis takes place.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.902
Thylakoids act as fat blockers,

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.938
delaying our digestion of fats

00:02:17.938 --> 00:02:22.142
and promoting the release
of satiety hormones like GLP-1.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.011
When we eat thylakoids,

00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:26.513
in other words, when we bite
into a leaf of spinach,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.614
for instance,

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.050
the thylakoid membranes
are able to resist

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.785
our digestive enzymes.

00:02:31.785 --> 00:02:33.353
They can last for hours
in our gut

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.888
before finally
being broken down,

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:38.592
and it is in those hours
when they work their magic.

00:02:38.592 --> 00:02:41.595
Thylakoids glom
onto tiny droplets of fat

00:02:41.595 --> 00:02:43.797
in our digestive tract,
and, in this way,

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:46.666
powerfully slow our digestion
of fat.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.603
And that means more GLP-1.

00:02:49.603 --> 00:02:52.072
Yes, GLP-1 is a hormone
that is being developed

00:02:52.072 --> 00:02:54.007
as an anti-obesity drug

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.410
(this was published two years
before Ozempic).

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.779
But thylakoids
can cause our natural,

00:02:58.779 --> 00:03:00.680
endogenous release of GLP-1,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.749
which is an easier
and more physiological way

00:03:02.749 --> 00:03:04.217
to enhance GLP-1 levels

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:07.020
to achieve satiety
and calorie balance.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.090
But does it
actually cut cravings?

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:14.094
Spinach extracts
were disguised in jam and juice

00:03:14.094 --> 00:03:17.531
to sneak thylakoids
undetected into meals,

00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:19.933
and those unwittingly eating
the equivalent

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:22.135
of about half a cup (100 g)
of cooked spinach

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.970
felt significantly less hungry

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.973
and more satiated
over the next few hours.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:30.243
Give someone the equivalent
of a shot of wheatgrass juice

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.512
or what they might get
in a "green drink"

00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:34.047
or green smoothie,

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.683
and not only do they feel
more satiated,

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:40.954
but their cravings for sweet,
salty, and fatty snacks,

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:43.390
such as potato chips,
chocolate, and cinnamon buns,

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.459
drop by about a third.

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:47.060
Feed them candy anyway,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:50.430
and those who unknowingly
had been snuck some spinach,

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:54.367
report liking the sweets
significantly less.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.837
The satiating power of greens
has been attributed

00:03:56.837 --> 00:03:58.538
to their high fiber
and water contents

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.673
and low calorie density,

00:03:59.673 --> 00:04:02.876
but the thylakoids
may be their secret weapon,

00:04:02.876 --> 00:04:05.645
presumably because of
the increased release of GLP-1

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:08.381
following
thylakoid supplementation.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.884
In a systematic review
of randomized controlled trials

00:04:10.884 --> 00:04:12.285
on the effects
of thylakoid intake

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.753
on appetite and weight loss,

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.856
hunger-suppressing effects
of thylakoids

00:04:15.856 --> 00:04:17.357
were reported in all studies

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.793
that directly measured
hunger and fullness.

00:04:19.793 --> 00:04:21.628
But what about the weight loss?

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:25.098
Would the GLP-induced reduction
of cravings and hunger

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.868
from greens
translate into losing pounds?

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.770
That’s what I’ll cover next.

